  {
    "id": "pepijn-kremers",
    "name": "Pepijn Kremers",
    "html": "<h1>Pepijn Kremers</h1>\n<p><strong>PhD Candidate @ TU Delft </strong></p><p>Pepijn Kremers received his Bachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering from Delft University of Technology in 2023. In 2025, he received his Master's degree in Computer &amp; Embedded Systems Engineering, also from Delft University of Technology. During his studies, he worked as a teaching assistant for courses, from these programs, covering telecommunications, signal processing, systems engineering, and software engineering.</p><p>Currently, he is a PhD candidate at the microelectronics department of Delft University of Technology. More specifically, he works both in the Lab of Efficient Machine Intelligence (EMI) within the ELCA research group, and at NXP Semiconductors in Eindhoven. His research interests include low-power computing, analog circuit calibration, AI accelerators, hardware/software co-design, and signal processing.</p><br/><br/>",
